  '<p class="gd-p">Keep an eye on email use against the daily limit, the nightly backup and the occasional error page.</p><section class="gd-task" id="email-backups-and-site-health-email" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Email log</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The banner shows today&#39;s emails against the daily limit. From 80, Admins get a notice; near the limit, digests and marketing wait first and booking and sign-in emails are held last.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Filter the Outbox: All, Queued, Held, Sent, Failed, Suppressed or Skipped.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open an email to <b class="gd-ui">Resend</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Suppressions: <b class="gd-ui">Suppress an address</b> stops all mail to it; <b class="gd-ui">Lift</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Text it instead</b> on a held or queued email sends it at once by text to the person&#39;s mobile, with the link to their page. The email still goes when the limit lifts.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>When the limit is reached, booking and pickup emails (the confirmation, the agreement and signing links, pickup details, the handover, payment links and signing codes) go by text on their own, once each. Sign-in then opens on the phone option, and signing codes are offered by text first. Turn it off in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">All settings</b> &gt; Site settings, Email limit.</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/messages</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-23-email-desktop-dad31712.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:56.5%;top:31.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:35.5%;top:41.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:81.9%;top:52.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.6%;top:22.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="email-backups-and-site-health-backups" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Backups</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The database is backed up every night, encrypted and test-restored on the spot. Kept: the last 7 nights and each Sunday of the last 4 weeks, with point-in-time recovery for the last week. Every night the retention keeps the backup storage under 70% of its free 10 GB.</li><li>Every Monday the newest backup is checked again: it must be under 30 hours old and restore cleanly.</li><li>A failed backup, or none for 30 hours, opens a site alert: an email (outside the quiet hours), a task and a line on To do. Tell your developer the same day.</li><li>Keep a copy of the backup key in the company password manager. Without it no backup can be read.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="email-backups-and-site-health-site-health-and-alerts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Site health and alerts</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">To do</b>, the Site health card at the bottom.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every 5 minutes the site checks itself: the home page, a car page, the sign-in page and the site&#39;s health check, and also emails, scheduled jobs, the nightly backup and Stripe payments.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each line shows Working, Problem, Waiting for the website deploy or Not checked yet, what was found and how many checks failed in the last 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Short problems, such as a single Error 1102, only show here and in your morning digest (&quot;Site check: 6 failed checks in the last 24 hours, no alert email&quot;).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An email goes to rent@carmacars.ca only for a real outage: a page failing every check for 15 minutes, emails failing for 30 minutes, the nightly backup failing, or Stripe failing for 30 minutes. It also raises an urgent task and &quot;Site problems found by the site check&quot; first on To do. A failed scheduled job is never emailed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">At most 3 alert emails a day, and none from 11 pm to 7 am unless the whole site has been down for an hour. An outage held overnight is emailed at 7 am if it lasts. One &quot;Recovered&quot; email follows each alert, and the task closes by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">&quot;Waiting for the website deploy&quot; on the health check means the database was updated before the website: nothing is wrong, and it turns to Working after the deploy.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The alert address, the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours are in Program settings, &quot;Site check&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="email-backups-and-site-health-when-a-page-shows-error-1102" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a page shows &quot;Error 1102&quot;</h2><p class="gd-p">Our web host&#39;s free plan sometimes stops a page that takes too long. Reload the page; you are still signed in. Moving to the Workers Paid plan removes it.</p></section>');
-- GUIDES 0322 END
